nstance: 1 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    cells = [(r, c) for r, row in enumerate(grid) for c, v in enumerate(row) if v == 8]\n    r0 = min(r for r, c in cells)\n    r1 = max(r for r, c in cells)\n    c0 = min(c for r, c in cells)\n    c1 = max(c for r, c in cells)\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    return [[grid[h - 1 - r][w - 1 - c] for c in range(c0, c1 + 1)]\n            for r in range(r0, r1 + 1)]\n```\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":22,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793566008.501,"t1":1793566028.181,"alias":"task-5e50dd96","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n9 9 1 4\n4 1 7 5\n1 4 5 7\n1 9 4 3\nwhere the pair's output is\n6 9 6 6\n9 3 9 9\n3 4 9 9\n1 9 4 1\nFailed checks in this instance: 2 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    cells = [(r, c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] == 8]\n    r0, r1 = min(r for r, c in cells), max(r for r, c in cells)\n    c0, c1 = min(c for r, c in cells), max(c for r, c in cells)\n\n    # The unmasked image repeats in reflected halves; use the reflected\n    # counterpart of the masked rectangle.\n    return [[grid[h - 1 - r][c] for c in range(c0, c1 + 1)]\n            for r in range(r0, r1 + 1)]\n```\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":22,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793566028.232,"t1":1793566044.692,"alias":"task-5e50dd96","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n3 4 9 9\n1 9 4 1\n3 1 1 4\n7 6 1 9\nwhere the pair's output is\n6 9 6 6\n9 3 9 9\n3 4 9 9\n1 9 4 1\nFailed checks in this instance: 3 of 3. Reply with a corrected progr